{"timestamp":"2026-09-01T07:47:46.651Z","ordinal":13764,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a05669-fc4c-7aa0-b9a1-034d833ed8ed","turn_id":"01a05bee-b4d9-7d91-9c13-042c2f3dc999","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8d5d5fc8-bc02-4137-a55d-dab0127bf30a","process_id":"2402","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","docker exec tiered-serve bash -lc 'sed -n \"1,75p\" /root/projects/tiered-serve/tiered_serve/dual_memory_loader/frozen_split.py; sed -n \"220,440p\" /root/projects/tiered-serve/tiered_serve/compression/core/chunk_delta3.py; sed -n \"1,180p\" /root/projects/tiered-serve/tiered_serve/model_configs/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct/cao-cd3-fused.yaml'"],"cwd":"file:///home/ubuntu","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"docker exec tiered-serve bash -lc 'sed -n \"1,75p\" /root/projects/tiered-serve/tiered_serve/dual_memory_loader/frozen_split.py; sed -n \"220,440p\" /root/projects/tiered-serve/tiered_serve/compression/core/chunk_delta3.py; sed -n \"1,180p\" /root/projects/tiered-serve/tiered_serve/model_configs/meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct/cao-cd3-fused.yaml'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import torch\nfrom tiered_serve.dual_memory_loader.base import *  # noqa: F401,F403\n\n\n# Per-codec prefill-alt chunk thresholds: the crossover N* below which the\n# alt-decode path (H2D compressed exp + reconstruct) beats the raw_bf16 fast\n# path (H2D 2*M*K, no kernel).  N* = (T_h2d_raw - T_dec) / t_gemm_per_token,\n# and ONLY T_dec (the codec's full-weight reconstruct cost) is codec-dependent:\n# a cheap branchless palette decode (p4flat) crosses over at a large chunk,\n# while a heavy ANS decode (dietgpu) crosses over at a much smaller one.\n# (zipserv is triple-bitmap exponent coding, NOT ANS; under frozen_split its\n# exp-only decode is cheap too, so it crosses over late — see the table below.)\n# Measure T_decomp per codec with benchmarks/weight_compress.py on an idle GPU\n# (its d_ms decompress-latency column, summed over the qkv/o/gateup/down fused\n# weights), feed it through the slack model above, and paste the result here.\n# Codecs absent from this dict fall back to\n# _PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK_GLOBAL_DEFAULT (= prior single-threshold behaviour).\n# The env var TIERED_SERVE_PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK overrides both: a single int\n# forces one global threshold; \"<codec>=<n>,...\" sets per-codec values.\n_PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK_GLOBAL_DEFAULT = 1330\n# Threshold = (T_load_raw_bf16 - T_decomp) / T_gemm_per_token, i.e. how many\n# tokens of GEMM fit in the slack the raw-H2D path has over the decode path.\n# This is CONFIG-AGGREGATE, not per-weight: T_load_raw and T_decomp depend on\n# the residency layout, so the SAME codec has different thresholds in different\n# configs. The values here are for the frozen_split configs (cao family);\n# offload_compressed configs use _OFFLOAD_PREFILL_MAX_CHUNK_DEFAULTS.\n#\n# Two effects make frozen_split (e.g. cao) carry a HIGH threshold:\n#   * frozen_split decode is EXP-ONLY (sm stays HBM) — far cheaper than the\n#     offload full-blob decompress, so T_decomp is small.\n#   * with all layers frozen_split, every layer loads raw (large T_load_raw).\n#   => big slack => large threshold.\n#   codec      thr    source\n#   p4flat     1330   hand-calibrated 400ms cao-p4flat operating point\n#                     (exp-only decomp 72 / load_raw 364 -> slack 292).\n#   chunk_delta3 1856 GH200/Llama-70B end-to-end forced-route sweep:\n#                     compressed standalone wins through N=1824; raw BF16\n#                     wins at N=1856 and every tested point through N=3072.\n#   zipserv    1107   cao slack model: load_raw 364 / exp-only decomp 121 ->\n#                     slack 243 -> 1330*243/292 = ~1107. zipserv's triple-\n#                     bitmap exp decode is HEAVIER than p4flat's palette\n#                     (121 vs 72ms), so it crosses over to raw_bf16 earlier.\n#   ublb_flat  1367   } synthetic isolated bench (palette/data-independent);\n#   p4d16      1206   } refine with the slack model if used under a real config.\n#   dietgpu     670   STALE synthetic. ANS+data-dependent — re-derive.\n_PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK_DEFAULTS = {\n    \"p4flat\": 1330,\n    \"chunk_delta3\": 1856,\n    \"ublb_flat\": 1367,\n    \"p4d16\": 1206,\n    \"zipserv\": 1107,   # cao (frozen_split): slack 243 (decomp 121) -> ~1107\n    \"dietgpu\": 670,    # TODO: re-derive with the slack model on a real config\n}\n\n# Codecs whose decompress is BIT-EXACT w.r.t. the original BF16 weight, so\n# decoding them during prefill is lossless. FP8 cells (zipserv_fp8, dietgpu_fp8,\n# p3flat_fp8) quantize, so offload_compressed prefill must keep their\n# uncompressed copy (see the \"for accuracy\" branch in _get_weight_source).\n_LOSSLESS_OFFLOAD_CODECS = frozenset({\n    \"zipserv\", \"dietgpu\", \"zipserv_bf16\", \"dietgpu_bf16\",\n    \"p4flat\", \"p4d16\", \"ublb_flat\",\n    \"chunk_delta3\",\n})\n\n# Phase-adaptive prefill for offload_compressed weights (see _get_weight_source).\n# offload_compressed already keeps BOTH a compressed and an uncompressed LPDDR\n# copy; today prefill ALWAYS H2Ds the uncompressed one (no chunk gating). Below\n# this per-codec chunk threshold, prefill instead H2Ds + FULL-decompresses the\n# compressed copy. Same slack model as the frozen_split knob\n# (thr = (T_load_raw - T_decomp)/T_gemm_per_token) but with DISTINCT inputs:\n# offload does the FULL-blob decompress (vs frozen_split's cheap exp-only), so\n# T_decomp is much larger, AND offload configs (e.g. flexgen-comp) typically\n# keep half the layers frozen_uncompressed, so fewer layers load -> smaller\n# T_load_raw. Both shrink the slack -> a MUCH lower threshold than frozen_split.\n#   codec    thr   source\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        comp_stream: Optional[torch.cuda.Stream] = None,\n        decomp_stream: Optional[torch.cuda.Stream] = None,\n    ):\n        super().__init__(comp_stream, decomp_stream)\n        if